User: A rectangular piece of paper $ABCD$ is folded so that edge $CD$ lies along edge $AD,$ making a crease $DP.$ It is unfolded, and then folded again so that edge $AB$ lies along edge $AD,$ making a second crease $AQ.$ The two creases meet at $R,$ forming triangles $PQR$ and $ADR$. If $AB=5\mbox{ cm}$ and $AD=8\mbox{ cm},$ what is the area of quadrilateral $DRQC,$ in $\mbox{cm}^2?$

[asy]
size(250);
draw((0,0)--(5,0)--(5,8)--(0,8)--cycle,black+linewidth(1));
draw((8,0)--(8,8)--(13,8)--(13,5)--(8,5),black+linewidth(1));
draw((8,0)--(13,5),black+linewidth(1)+dashed);
draw((16,0)--(21,0)--(21,8)--(16,8)--cycle,black+linewidth(1));
draw((16,0)--(21,5),black+linewidth(1)+dashed);
draw((16,8)--(21,3),black+linewidth(1)+dashed);
draw((12,0)--(10,2),black+linewidth(1));
draw((12,0)--(10,2),EndArrow);
label("$A$",(0,8),N);
label("$B$",(5,8),N);
label("$C$",(5,0),S);
label("$D$",(0,0),S);
label("$A$",(8,8),N);
label("$B$",(13,8),N);
label("$C$",(8,5),W);
label("$D$",(8,0),S);
label("$P$",(13,5),E);
label("$A$",(16,8),N);
label("$B$",(21,8),N);
label("$C$",(21,0),S);
label("$D$",(16,0),S);
